DROPS Red Zone Monitoring

This public repository contains application source code for local red-zone monitoring.
It does not include videos, customer data, signing certificates, Apple credentials, or YOLO model binaries.

Third-party components include:

- Ultralytics YOLO tooling and models. Users must obtain/export model weights locally and comply with Ultralytics license terms.
- ONNX Runtime Web, used for browser inference runtime assets.
- Next.js, React, Tailwind CSS, and related npm packages for the web app.
- Python, OpenCV, PySide6, PyTorch, and Ultralytics dependencies for the native Mac app.

The browser expects a locally generated model at `public/models/yolo26n.onnx`.
The native Mac app can download/use `yolo26n.pt` locally through Ultralytics tooling during development or packaging.
